ty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-128353/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e0b4d33-7699-5068-90f1-663534cd662d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128353"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-18658/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "1e83007f-d2c6-5839-9037-7656b6766b65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18658/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "a97dd138-70f2-5d39-8ba1-22919ce2fa27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18658/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "c16e8bc2-ebc8-5175-85b1-ab014e408913" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18658/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "d31af9ee-b637-534f-b2ef-8fc4ae864f4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18658/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "93887c8c-3dd7-5829-88d6-832b484164cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18658/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0bd0ac1c-3cb4-51e7-aa4a-416abf6f0134" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-18658/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-18658/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-18658/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-18658/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-18658/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-18658/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-18658" :question/id #uuid "3510e83f-4adc-58a8-b3a5-d0db2be677d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-18658" :question/problem "Find $b\\cdot (a\\times c)$, if $4a\\cdot (-b\\times c)=12.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4a\\cdot (-b\\times c) & =12 \\\\ 4\\cdot (-1)\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =12 \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (a\\times c) & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-18658/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e0b4d33-7699-5068-90f1-663534cd662d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-18658"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73470/selection/94b1e608a1bece13c117321c62644f2051416b0003719c2dd4b9ea44af9d6b64" :answer/id #uuid "7c36065e-c546-5040-892d-0afeb58e039c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73470/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer/id #uuid "d27156bd-b73a-55a3-8410-555a0fa4c033" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73470/selection/2fa5baf88b61736a3022c72e24e172fda2b4270fffff6efaa1fc03fef23fccc2" :answer/id #uuid "b10548b2-ba23-57c9-8e9f-efb6408540fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73470/selection/594f4371237f716a4e7b771cfac6a2ca8b8eb3c8dcb7752f2b3291728275476a" :answer/id #uuid "882fee4d-a313-5036-8aa0-6990f6344c53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73470/selection/aa57a8d17f569b619e62bd602a6af7cff5d106888256da51f23b5b66e6987fe8" :answer/id #uuid "257852e8-5d5a-5e0d-bf36-26c0bddadb95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73470/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3bf5f324-5e79-5cde-aeed-51d58a38a052" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73470/selection/aa57a8d17f569b619e62bd602a6af7cff5d106888256da51f23b5b66e6987fe8" :answer-field/choices ["q-73470/selection/94b1e608a1bece13c117321c62644f2051416b0003719c2dd4b9ea44af9d6b64" "q-73470/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" "q-73470/selection/2fa5baf88b61736a3022c72e24e172fda2b4270fffff6efaa1fc03fef23fccc2" "q-73470/selection/594f4371237f716a4e7b771cfac6a2ca8b8eb3c8dcb7752f2b3291728275476a" "q-73470/selection/aa57a8d17f569b619e62bd602a6af7cff5d106888256da51f23b5b66e6987fe8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73470" :question/id #uuid "6b76eac9-1fca-591a-8edf-8b517293adda" :question/math-academy-id "q-73470" :question/problem "Find $c\\cdot (b\\times a)$, if $b\\times c=⟨3,-1,2⟩$ and $a=⟨4,-2,6⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the triple scalar product \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨4,-2,6⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+6\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =12+2+12 \\\\  & =26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a)=-26.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73470/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e0b4d33-7699-5068-90f1-663534cd662d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73470"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4347"] :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 2,-3,2 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -1,0,5 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle 1,2,3 \\rangle.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the cross product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\times c & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 3-5\\cdot 2)i-(-1\\cdot 3-5\\cdot 1)j+(-1\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =-10i+8j-2k \\\\  & =⟨-10,8,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the scalar triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨2,-3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-10,8,-2⟩ \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-10)+(-3)\\cdot 8+2\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-48\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4348"] :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 4,2,-1 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,2,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,-1,2 \\rangle.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the scalar triple product $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c})$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $\\mathbf{a},$ $\\mathbf{b},$ and $\\mathbf{c}.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot (2\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-1))-2\\cdot (0\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-1))+(-1)\\cdot (0\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =20-2-2 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4349"] :question/problem "Find $\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}),$ if $2\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times 3\\mathbf{c}) = 5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a\\cdot (b\\times 3c) & =5 \\\\ 2\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times 3c)] & =5 \\\\ 2\\cdot 3\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =5 \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a) & =-\\frac{5}{6},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand again we swap $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (a\\times b) & =\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
